Added after the fact, because this is what this file is for.

**Demolished, by us, within a day of writing it down.** `desire/` wished the two
economies would stay separate forever, and said that every game like this
eventually grows an exchange rate between its currencies. The reroll is that
exchange rate. Nobody argued against the prediction; the design simply walked
into it while looking at something else, and the argument for the reroll was good
on its own terms.

The useful part is not that the wish lost. It is *how* it lost: not to a bad
decision, but to a good one made in a different room. Which is the thing to watch
for -- the next exchange rate will also arrive attached to a reasonable idea, and
it will not announce itself as an exchange rate either.
